  "name": "discover-layer-implementation-types",
  "description": "A `discover` narrowed to one layer, answered at full fidelity: every element kind of `implementation_types`, every declared field with its type, its `required`/`immutable` flags (each published where it is `true`: in this default `summary` form an absent one means `false`), enum members, declared unit and reference target, and the nested member kinds a `create` inside an element addresses. This is the round trip that lets a client author a data type it has never seen a tool for.",
  "kind": "example",
